      "rubric_id": "R4",
      "class": "decision-now",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "affected_surface": "src/runners/review-packet.js (materializePacket) and §1.2.2 of the plan under review",
      "claim": "The proposed per-seat materialisation via hardlink copy ('cp -al', with 'plain copy' only as a fallback) does not guarantee that no seat can write into another seat's view: hardlinked regular files share the inode, so a tools-capable seat that appends to or overwrites a packet file in place mutates the bytes every other seat sees, and the shared build's hash silently diverges from what any seat actually read.",
      "evidence": "Plan §1.2.2 states each seat launches against its own copy of the built packet directory via 'hardlink or reflink copy, cp -al/--reflink=auto fallback to plain copy'; §2.2 lists 'materializePacket(src, dst)' in review-packet.js. A hardlink is not a private copy for content writes; only file replacement (unlink+create) is isolated, and the plan never requires copy-on-write or unlink-before-write semantics, nor a post-materialisation hash check per seat dir.",
      "evidence_reference": "PLAN_UNDER_REVIEW §1.2.2 (\"hardlink or reflink copy, cp -al/--reflink=auto fallback to plain copy\") and §2.2 (materializePacket)",
      "repair": "Decide now: materialise with plain per-file copies (or reflink where the filesystem guarantees it), or if hardlinks are kept for cost, require a post-materialisation verify (re-hash the seat's directory against the shared packet_hash) plus a documented write-isolation contract before any seat launch; pin it in review-packet.test.sh with a test that mutates a file in one seat dir and asserts the other seat dirs and the shared hash are unaffected.",
